  "result": "The fix is in `src/server/services/notification-service.ts`, in `notify()`. The loop over recipients now skips any recipient whose id equals `payload.actorId`, so the person who triggered the event no longer gets a notification for it.\n\nThe cause: the `comment.created` subscriber builds the watcher list from the issue's author and assignee and passes it to `notify()`. `notify()` never compared the recipients against the actor, so when you commented on an issue you were assigned, you were in that list and got the notification. The existing test \"does not notify the actor about their own action\" expected this exclusion but could not pass without it.\n\nThe check sits in the shared `notify()` path, so it applies to every event kind, not just comments. I did not run the test suite.",
